t he's riding around in one of those bodies but I wouldn't be surprised if that's out there, possibly in one of the older Conv. Books. I can take a look later if you're still curious. I think the stuff about the clone and the other dude both get mentions in Guide to the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:30:20-07:00","id":993770,"title":"","content":"SPOILERS<br /> <br /> I believe that would be Tychoides, the Void Engineer who got his mind transferred to a young clone of himself every time his current body died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T06:32:00-07:00","id":994008,"title":"","content":"Thanx guys, I haven't had a chance ro check all these out yet (work) but you've given me the places to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T07:27:30-07:00","id":994020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OmegaZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993279-wolfgang-von-reisman-or-who?p=993770#post993770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SPOILERS<br /> <br /> I believe that would be Tychoides, the Void Engineer who got his mind transferred to a young clone of himself every time his current body died.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what Progenitors do as well. Is Tychoides any different?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T18:53:51-07:00","id":995470,"title":"","content":"Where is Riesman's son mentioned. Its what i can't seem to find","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:19:27-07:00","id":995618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993279-wolfgang-von-reisman-or-who#post993279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been wracking my brain to remember which of the old leaders/founders of the Order of Reason extended his life by being reborn as his own lineage. At least I think that's how I remember it being done. I might be putting a few people together but I thought it was also the same person who formed the Craftmasons. Whitewolfwiki has been no help and I've gone through nearly everything from the Dark Age's books to M20 and cant find it mentioned. I know I've read it. Any Ideas?<br /> <br /> Thanx</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Wolfgang Von Reisman was a big leader in the Brotherhood of the Rule/La Compagnia, the group that would become the High Guild and the Syndicate. He and the Brotherhood were involved with Craftmasons as they were forming themselves. They paid for the mercenary soldiers the Craftmasons used at Mistridge and a century later, helped them reach out to various other Philosopher-Scientist groups, forming the Order of Reason. In-universe, the High Guild/Syndicate rewrote history once the Craftmasons were disbanded, attributing their accomplishments to themselves and claiming that they created the Craftmasons.<br /> <br /> As for Von Reisman's son, he's not talked about. The 1E Syndicate CB also talks about Joseph von Reisman, one of Wolfgang's descendants, who is the VPO of Europe West in the pre-Avatar Storm. He disappeared like much of the Union's leadership in the Storm.<br /> <br /> The status of the old leaders/founders of the Order of Reason is largely unknown as the only time they've ever clearly explained Control, the top of the Union's pyramid was in <i>Ascension</i> and in that book we got to different versions of Control, depending on the scenario. One it's a faceless, formless force created by the paranoid subconscious beliefs of the Union while in the other Control is the original founders of the Order forced off Earth because of the Paradox of their life-prolonging Procedures and because of getting cut off by the Avatar Storm have basically become Spirits of Reason.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:58:06-07:00","id":995657,"title":"","content":"The Guide to the Tech mention for Jacob is on page 69, detailing Wolfgang's eventual death. In addition to showing up in the Synd book, Joseph has a short bio in the Synd section of Guide to the Technocracy (pg 117). Jacob certainly feels like a thing that'd get more mention elsewhere, but it may just be one of those things that fell by the wayside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:22:47-07:00","id":995669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993279-wolfgang-von-reisman-or-who?p=995657#post995657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guide to the Tech mention for Jacob is on page 69, detailing Wolfgang's eventual death. In addition to showing up in the Synd book, Joseph has a short bio in the Synd section of Guide to the Technocracy (pg 117). Jacob certainly feels like a thing that'd get more mention elsewhere, but it may just be one of those things that fell by the wayside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, he was one of the VPOs, a member of the Syndicate's Board of Directors. So he was a big deal but then the Avatar Storm happened and the entire Board was lost. Since then they've reorganized and the Syndicate has a new set of VPOs to lead the Convention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:28:49-07:00","id":995672,"title":"","content":"...yeah? Joseph is/was. I don't know what you think you're clarifying?<br /> <br /> <i>Jacob </i>is the clone &quot;son&quot; that I don't recall any further mention of. <i>He</i> wasn't a VPO and while it's likely he'd also be gone in the Reckoning I don't really know where he was or what his effective rank was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:01:58-07:00","id":996326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993279-wolfgang-von-reisman-or-who?p=995672#post995672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...yeah? Joseph is/was. I don't know what you think you're clarifying?<br /> <br /> <i>Jacob </i>is the clone &quot;son&quot; that I don't recall any further mention of. <i>He</i> wasn't a VPO and while it's likely he'd also be gone in the Reckoning I don't really know where he was or what his effective rank was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joseph, as he was the one I was talking about in the post just before yours.<br /> <br /> The clone, Jacob, I only ever recall him from GttT. But as that entry points out, Jacob was a clone but not a clone-body inhabited by Wolfgang's consciousness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}